# Linear issue status after work

When you finish the work for a Linear issue in this repo, set that issue to **In Review**. Do not leave it In Progress. Do not mark it Done.

## When this applies

- The issue’s acceptance criteria are met (or you have a PR / commit that implements the scoped work).
- You are wrapping up the session for that issue.

## How

Use the Linear MCP `save_issue` tool (or the Linear UI/CLI if MCP is unavailable):

- `id`: the issue identifier (e.g. `APP-130`)
- `state`: `In Review`

Apps team status names: Backlog, Todo, In Progress, **In Review**, Done.

## Do not

- Mark the issue **Done** (a human reviews first).
- Move a different issue, or a parent epic, unless that was the work you completed.
- Skip the status update because the branch is unpushed. Update Linear when the work is complete in the working tree / PR.
